          <p>Kneading is a common comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood during nursing. Adult cats may keep doing it when they feel safe, sleepy, or are claiming a cozy spot with their scent glands.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4" id="faq-button-4">
          <span>Do indoor cats still need enrichment?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="faq-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-button-4" hidden>
          <p>Yes. Indoor cats benefit from climbing spaces, scratching posts, puzzle feeders, window views, and interactive play sessions that let them stalk, chase, and pounce safely every day.</p>
        </div>
